}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    shape: square, N x N where N = L*C + (L-1), 27-30
    L: lattice dimension (rows and cols of cells), 4-6
    C: cell size (square), 4-6
  separator:
    single color, forms all full-span rows and full-span columns
    single-pixel-wide lines, evenly spaced (gap = C+1)
    count: L-1 rows and L-1 columns
    sep color does not appear inside any cell
  lattice_cells:
    total: L x L square grid of C x C cells
    each cell is either solid (monochrome, all pixels one color) or pattern (>=2 colors)
  solid_block:
    contiguous rectangle in lattice coords, 2-3 rows x 2-3 cols
    each solid cell filled with a single color; >=2 distinct colors across the block [observed]
    may touch lattice border (test_0 does)
  pattern_cells:
    all non-solid cells; each uses >=5 distinct colors [observed]
    cells with same (ri-ci) value share identical content [observed]
    content is structured (e.g. Toeplitz-like) but solver only requires non-monochrome
  output: colors of the solid cells arranged by lattice position, shape = solid_block shape

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick L in 4-6, C in 4-6; compute N = L*C + (L-1)
    2. Choose 1 separator color (sep)
    3. Build the output (solid block): pick solid_h in 2-3, solid_w in 2-3; pick top-left
       lattice position so the block fits within L x L; fill with random colors != sep
    4. Build a base pattern tile (C x C) using >=3 colors all != sep; for each lattice
       diagonal (ri-ci) mod (2*L-1) generate a distinct tile variant (e.g. cyclic shift
       or random permutation of the base)
    5. Assemble grid: place sep lines at positions C, 2C+1, 3C+2, ...; fill each
       non-solid lattice cell with its diagonal's pattern tile; fill solid cells with
       their monochrome color
    6. Verify: every full-span row/col is sep-colored, every pattern cell has >=2 colors,
       solid block is contiguous rectangle
